WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.669
Welcome back to State of the Union.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.636
The January six

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.672
committee is set to release its report

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.306
next month,

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.474
but some staff say

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.642
it may not represent all their findings.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.544
Sources told The Washington Post

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.078
that they felt

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.480
Republican Congresswoman Liz

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.049
Cheney was only interested in evidence

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.184
that pertained to former President Trump,

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.487
which prompted a fire response

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.323
from a spokesperson for Cheney

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:25.558
and also one from the committee.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:28.261
Here with me now to discuss January six

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.830
and a lot of other issues

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.499
is a member of that committee,

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.733
Democrat Adam Schiff.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.169
Thank you so much for coming in.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.871
Let's start with that Post report,

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.407
which was a really remarkable report.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.875
Staffers were told

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.476
the final January six report

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.444
would likely

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.713
almost entirely focus on Donald Trump,

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.648
potentially leaving out

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.884
a significant amount of your committee's

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.553
report and investigation, other areas.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.522
That's what The Post said. Is it true?

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.390
No.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.492
I mean, I certainly hope not.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.660
I would like to see our report

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.762
be as broad and inclusive as possible.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.165
We are discussing as a committee

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.533
among the members

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.101
what belongs in the body of the report,

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:08.701
what belongs

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.770
in the appendices of the report.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.404
What is beyond

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.907
the scope of our investigation?

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.276
And we'll reach those decisions

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.079
in a collaborative manner.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:19.379
You know,

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.580
I think the one of the things

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.414
that has made our committee

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.850
so successful is we have worked extremely

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.751
well together.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:25.185
That doesn't mean

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.619
we always agree on everything,

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.320
but it does mean

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.122
we have a lot of respect for each other.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.757
And we get to the

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.324
the goal,

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.525
which is

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.660
providing the American people

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.894
with a full accounting of what

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.496
took place on January six.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.464
That has certainly been

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.232
the public perception of it

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.534
and the public face of the committee.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.136
But it sounds like

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.337
there's a different story,

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.972
at least in some parts of the committee

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.340
behind the scenes.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:47.974
Liz Cheney,

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.375
spokesman, put out a statement

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.778
accusing staffers on that very committee

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.145
on her own

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.847
committee of trying to slip,

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.282
quote, liberal biases into the report.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.184
Here's what this quote said,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:58.751
that Cheney

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.520
won't sign on to any narrative

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.788
that suggests Republicans

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.022
are inherently racist

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.124
or smears men and women

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.025
in law enforcement or suggests

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.760
every American who believes

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.595
God has blessed

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.296
America is a white supremacist.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:10.797
And then

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.764
a committee spokesman

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.099
accused disgruntled

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.268
staffers of, quote, cowardice and said

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:15.902
they're helping

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:16.836
Donald Trump and others

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.104
responsible for the violence

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.005
of January six.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.341
That's a remarkable statement.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:21.975
They are

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:22.308
you know,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.610
I don't think the back and forth

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.511
is particularly helpful.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.678
The committee and I don't

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:26.546
want to engage in that.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.214
We're going to get to a

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.582
consensus on the report.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.317
We're very close to that now.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.685
We're close to the putting down

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.021
the pen and go into print.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:35.922
And I think the report

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.057
is going to set out in a

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.927
I hope, very comprehensive way.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.962
What took place, what led to that attack

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.232
and and all the circumstances around

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:46.833
that.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:47.767
We're also going to be

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.135
releasing the evidence,

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.104
which may be the most important thing,

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.372
the voluminous transcripts,

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.541
the documents and emails.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.742
We want to make sure that that's

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.677
put before the American people.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.312
We certainly don't want the Jim

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.814
Jordan's of the world to cherry pick

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.149
anything not disclosed

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:03.983
and make a false

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.852
or misleading narrative out of it.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.253
So the country is going to have

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.121
the evidence

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.023
they're going to have our report.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.558
And I'm enormously proud

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.225
of what we've done

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.127
and we'll be proud of the final result.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.161
Well, I was going to ask you about that.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.729
Jim Jordan has already said that

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.398
he is going to

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.332
he will be the chairman

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.500
of the Judiciary Committee.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.801
He is likely

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.369
he is going to go through the evidence

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:23.970
you left out.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:24.437
You're saying that

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.005
there won't be evidence

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.074
that will not be made public.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.709
The evidence will all be made public.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:32.412
Now, we'll have to make sure that

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:32.946
we scrub

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.948
that evidence for personally identifiable

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.482
information, that the evidence

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.018
that we provide protects people's

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.421
security.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.989
Does it put them at risk?

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.890
So there are things

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.591
that we're going to have to do

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:46.392
along those lines.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:47.694
But but, yes,

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:48.962
we want to put the evidence

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.163
before the American people,

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.598
which supports

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:53.499
the hearings that we've done,

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.168
as well as the report that we'll put out

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.970
and will be a comprehensive picture.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.771
A few weeks after January six,

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.306
you said the attack on the Capitol

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.041
was, quote, a massive intelligence

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.576
and security failure

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.745
that needs to be fully investigated.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.513
There were nine public hearings.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:10.483
None had a specific focus on

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.352
exactly that, on the security

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:13.920
and intelligence failures.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.154
Will those be detailed

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.756
in the final report?

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.757
I certainly hope they will,

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.592
and I'm advocating for that.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.361
I think that's part of the broad picture

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:21.794
of why

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.631
the Capitol was vulnerable to attack.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:25.698
What intelligence

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.201
we had, what intelligence we missed,

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.235
what intelligence was put

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.004
before law enforcement.

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.038
Are you meeting resistance?

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.039
I'm getting that in.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:33.273
You know,

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:33.706
I don't want to go

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.708
into our internal discussions

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.011
I think we'll get to common agreement.

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:39.712
Part of it is, you know,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.314
what belongs in the body of the report,

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.683
what belongs in the separate appendices.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.718
You know, what can be corroborated

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:47.720
We want to make sure that we have

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.555
every fact nailed down.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:50.690
That's been part of the reason

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.358
our committee has been so successful.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.060
And we want it to continue to be.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:54.661
I want to move on.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.528
But before I do,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.297
there does seem to be tension

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.865
surrounding the vice chair

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.867
of the committee, Liz Cheney.

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:01.567
One former

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.136
staffer told The Washington Post

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.804
that people working for the committee

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.539
became quote, discouraged

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:07.240
when they felt

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:07.940
it had become

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.244
a, quote, Cheney 20, 24 campaign affair.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.613
I've never viewed it that way.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:14.947
And I think her role on

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.516
the committee has been indispensable.

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.284
I have tremendous respect for her

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.219
and for Adam Kinzinger.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:20.853
They've shown

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.989
a lot of courage and backbone

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.624
as something in very short supply.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.359
In the GOP these days.

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:28.294
So the committee not would not have been

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:28.628
the same

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:30.663
without both of their participation.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:33.366
And and I have nothing but respect

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:34.200
for both of them.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.101
As you well know,

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.770
the man who was trying to be speaker.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:41.341
Republican Kevin McCarthy, says that he

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:42.842
wants to kick you off

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:43.776
the Intelligence Committee,

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:46.045
the committee that you now chair

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.747
because of your handling of the Trump

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.949
Russia investigation, and specifically

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.352
that you repeatedly asserted that

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.486
there was direct evidence

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:55.755
of collusion and direct collusion

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.323
which didn't materialize.

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:59.325
What's your response to McCarthy?

00:05:59.325 --> 00:05:59.926
Well, McCarthy

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.527
apparently doesn't think it's collusion.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.795
If your campaign manager

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.163
is giving inside polling

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.866
data and battle strategy in key states

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.768
to engage in Russian intelligence

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:09.502
while the Russians

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:10.403
are helping your campaign.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:11.437
But most Americans

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.172
would call that collusion.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.474
McCarthy's problem is not with

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:15.641
what I've said about Russia.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.410
McCarthy's problem is

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.278
he can't get to to 18

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.847
without Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:23.149
and Paul Gosar and Matt Gaetz.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.884
And so he will do whatever they ask.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.252
And right now,

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:26.953
they're asking for me

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:28.087
to be removed from my committees.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.122
And he's willing to do it.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.190
He's willing to do anything they ask.

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:32.225
And that's the problem.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:36.028
Kevin McCarthy has no ideology.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:38.564
He has no core set of beliefs.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:39.265
It's very hard

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:41.367
only to get to to a team that way.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.669
It's even more difficult to keep to 18.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:44.804
That's his problem.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:47.273
So he will misrepresent my record.

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:48.574
He'll misrepresent Eric

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:51.244
Swalwell or Ilhan Omar or whatever

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:52.111
he needs to do

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:55.448
to get the votes of the QAnon caucus

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:56.883
within this conference.

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:57.817
He's not the only one.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.952
The incoming oversight chair.

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.688
James Comer told Punchbowl

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:03.689
News in an interview.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:04.257
I don't believe

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.525
congressional investigations

00:07:05.525 --> 00:07:06.959
have a whole lot of credibility now.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:08.694
I blame Adam Schiff for that.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.229
But it's also both parties

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:12.365
to blame for investigations in the past.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:13.633
I want to change that.

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:14.400
What's your response?

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.135
Well, Coburn doesn't believe

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.270
in the Russia investigation.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:17.904
He doesn't believe

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.038
in the Ukraine investigation.

00:07:19.038 --> 00:07:20.640
He doesn't believe in the investigation.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.642
January 6th and why?

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:24.410
Because those are investigations

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.712
of the serial abuse

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:27.146
of power

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:30.316
by Donald Trump and Colmer and Jordan

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.584
and McCarthy

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:32.752
will do nothing but carry

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:33.920
Donald Trump's water.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.521
Someone, as you point out,

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.190
who is sitting down for dinner

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.825
with anti-Semites,

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:39.992
who's sitting down for dinner

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:42.829
with bigots, who won't condemn them.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:44.530
This is

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.932
who they're making common cause with.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:46.933
And so they will do.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:47.333
And what

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.568
and they will say what they need

00:07:48.568 --> 00:07:49.902
to get along with Donald Trump.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:50.436
We're out of time.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:52.038
But I just have to ask,

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:54.140
if you are subpoenaed

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.007
by Republicans

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.376
when they take over where you can play.

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:57.810
You know what?

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.678
We'll have to consider

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:00.446
the validity of the subpoena

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:02.982
but I would certainly view my obligation,

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.150
the administration's obligation

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.952
to follow the law

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.787
and the fact that they have disrespected

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:10.056
the law is not a precedent

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:10.523
I would hope

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:11.791
that would be broadly followed.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.593
But we'll have to look at the legitimacy

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.394
or lack of legitimacy of what they do.

